  "wideningMeanShiftCap": {
    "configuredCap": 1.5,
    "rationale": "Widening a right-skewed range raises its arithmetic mean because the upper tail is expanded while the most-likely value is held. Left unbounded, an Unknown answer would inflate the central estimate instead of merely widening the distribution. Widening is therefore reduced until the mean of the range is at most 1.5x the un-widened mean. The cap is applied by QkModifiers::applyRange to every widened input, and it is what keeps an all-Unknown assessment's central estimate within a stated multiple of the all-known assessment.",
